---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import business from '../data/business.json';
import catalog from '../data/catalog.json';
import { photos } from '../lib/images';
import { formatMoney } from '../lib/pricing';
import { breadcrumb, graph } from '../lib/schema';

const jsonLd = graph(Astro.site, [
  breadcrumb(Astro.site, [
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
  ]),
]);
---

<Base
  title="About the studio | Stitch & Stella"
  description="Stitch & Stella is named for Stella, a goldendoodle in Houston. The studio also stitches bandanas for Allie, a bernedoodle, and Mack, a mini Australian shepherd."
  image={photos.stella}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-14 md:grid-cols-2 md:py-20">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-rose-800">The studio</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-5xl leading-tight">Named Stella. Stitched in Houston.</h1>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-soft">
        <p>
          Stitch &amp; Stella makes one thing: a dog bandana cut to a neck measurement and finished with an edge you can point at. Stella is the goldendoodle the studio is named for. Allie is a bernedoodle. Mack is a mini Australian shepherd. The name on the cloth can be any dog’s.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no shop floor. Saturday mornings are the Heights handoff, 77008 and 77009. Thursday evenings are the Garden Oaks drop, 77018. The rest of the week is for stitching and for answering tickets.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cloth is {business.materials.join(', ').toLowerCase()}. Halloween and Christmas use the same weight of cotton. A Houston December does not get a fleece bandana from this studio.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Image
      src={photos.stella}
      alt="Stella, a cream goldendoodle, on a couch in a pink gingham bandana stitched with red hearts and the name Stella."
      widths={[480, 800]}
      sizes="(min-width: 768px) 32rem, 100vw"
      quality={60}
      format="avif"
      loading="eager"
      class="h-auto w-full rounded-3xl"
    />
  </article>

  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-14 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">Care</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 leading-7 text-ink-soft">
          {business.care.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">Safety</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 leading-7 text-ink-soft">
          {business.safety.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl">Not included</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 leading-7 text-ink-soft">
          {business.notIncluded.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">What a ticket is</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-ink-soft">
      The designer writes down the cloth, the stitch, and the price. The ticket page puts your name and handoff on it and opens an email to {business.email}. The same facts are published as a catalog file so a search engine or an assistant can quote the studio without guessing. A handmade bandana starts at {formatMoney(catalog.basePriceCents)}. The lead time is {catalog.leadDays} studio days, longer for an heirloom edge.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
